SUMMARY:(4209) Briggs hides a mag 12.8 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(4209) Briggs hides a magnitude 12.8 star\, seen from Bannu\, P
 K.\nThe predicted edge passes 11 km to the W\, so a miss is likely — but
  a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClos
 est approach 02:28:50 PKT\, give or take 1 s. The star is 63° up in the N
 E · dark sky.\nIt fades 4.2 magnitudes for up to 2.4 s on the centre line
 \, and the path is 31 km wide\, give or take 20 km.\nFinder chart\, the ma
 p and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-
 13-4209-briggs-439936
