SUMMARY:(1792) Reni hides a mag 12.2 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(1792) Reni hides a magnitude 12.2 star\, seen from Bannu\, PK.
 \nThe predicted edge passes 11 km to the NNW\, so a miss is likely — but
  a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClos
 est approach 04:45:11 PKT\, give or take 1 s. The star is 50° up in the E
  · dark sky.\nIt fades 4.2 magnitudes for up to 0.8 s on the centre line\
 , and the path is 24 km wide\, give or take 16 km.\nFinder chart\, the map
  and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2027-08#2027-08-2
 4-1792-reni-338816
